{
	chapter.06FC482FE2685079.title: "The Locomotive Age"
	chapter.245A4F185E1B81C3.title: "Introduction"
	chapter.31661C695EDB8A71.title: "The Copper Age"
	chapter.50DB8B06FCC52596.title: "Post Production"
	chapter.586695A8DC168300.title: "The Brass Age"
	chapter.6D4F1AE8D4C9E4FD.title: "Milestones"
	chapter.711371031CAB5D28.title: "Basic Progression"
	chapter.7BCE7E5AB3995620.title: "The Andesite Age"
	chapter_group.72E1283473A995A4.title: "Time to Create"
	file.0000000000000001.title: "Everyone Creates"
	quest.01FD0A43E4128D6A.quest_desc: [
		"Taking items out of an &6Item Vault&r with an &6Andesite Funnel&r can be rather inefficient and inconvenient, so let’s try something better."
		""
		"The &6Packager&r lets you bundle up to nine stacks of items into a single &6Package&r from almost any type of storage container."
		""
		"You can unpack a Package directly from your inventory by holding it in your main hand and using &6Shift + Right-Click&r. Doing so will unpack its contents into your inventory and consume the Package."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"This still does not solve the problem of choosing which items to take out of an &6Item Vault&r. This is where the &6Stock Ticker&r comes in."
		""
		"Place the Stock Ticker and position a &6Seat&r with any mob seated on it next to the Stock Ticker. That mob will become your &6Stock Keeper&r. You can also use a &6Blaze Burner&r as your Stock Keeper, but this requires a trip to the &6Nether&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Next, right-click the &6Stock Ticker&r with a &6Stock Link&r to tune it, then place the tuned Stock Link against a &6Packager&r that is attached to a container, such as an Item Vault."
		""
		"The Stock Ticker is now linked to the Packager's container through the Stock Link, creating a &6Logistics Network&r. The container becomes accessible through the &6Stock Keeper&r, so you can view all the items stored inside it."
		""
		"To add more containers to this Logistics Network, tune the same Stock Ticker with additional Stock Links and place them against the Packagers you want to link."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Now let’s place an &6Order&r through the &6Logistics Network&r. Interact with the &6Stock Keeper&r and choose the items you want to retrieve from the linked storage. Press send to confirm your order."
		""
		"A &6Package&r will then be created by the Packager containing the requested items. If you request more items than can fit in a single Package, additional Packages will be created automatically."
		""
		"Use an &6Andesite Funnel&r to move the Packages onto a &6Mechanical Belt&r and transport them to your desired pick-up point."
		""
		"Take a look at the final pages for images showing an example of this setup."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Opening the &6Stock Ticker&r’s interface lets you create &6Categories&r. These act as filters that group items together, dividing the list shown through the Stock Keeper into custom-named sections."
		""
		"Categories are created using either a &6List Filter&r or an &6Attribute Filter&r. A List Filter lets you manually select specific items, while an Attribute Filter groups items based on their properties."
		""
		"You can even place one List Filter inside another List Filter, which in theory allows you to include an unlimited number of items in a single category."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/package1.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/package2.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/package3.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
	]
	quest.01FD0A43E4128D6A.quest_subtitle: "Setting Up a Stock Network"
	quest.01FD0A43E4128D6A.title: "The Packager and Stock Links"
	quest.0577084B1A9752AE.quest_subtitle: "From First Motion to Full Mastery"
	quest.0577084B1A9752AE.title: "Master Engineer"
	quest.09B8DFE47D682A97.quest_desc: ["Use the &6Sleeping Bag&r to sleep anywhere without resetting your &6Respawn Point&r."]
	quest.09B8DFE47D682A97.quest_subtitle: "Time to Set Your Respawn Point"
	quest.09B8DFE47D682A97.title: "The Bed"
	quest.0B10074131B65420.quest_subtitle: "Mastering Smart Automation"
	quest.0B10074131B65420.title: "Completing the Brass Age"
	quest.0BA7D7070792D58C.quest_desc: [
		"Using Campfires to heat a Boiler does not provide much benefit over Water Wheels or Windmills, so let’s look at a more powerful heat source: &6Blaze Burners&r."
		""
		"When fueled, Blaze Burners produce far more heat than Campfires. This allows the Boiler to reach a higher level, which increases its &6Stress Capacity&r. Make sure you supply enough water to keep up with the increased heat."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To increase the heat even further, fuel a Blaze Burner with a &6Blaze Cake&r. This &6Superheats&r the Blaze Burner, allowing the Boiler to reach even higher Boiler Levels and greatly increase the Steam Engine’s output."
	]
	quest.0BA7D7070792D58C.quest_subtitle: "Super-Heating Blaze Burners"
	quest.0BA7D7070792D58C.title: "The Blaze Cake"
	quest.0BC9416C2B7C8D5E.quest_desc: [
		"In the &6Andesite Age&r, you learned several ways to automate item processing, such as producing Bread or setting up &6Bulk Blasting&r. All of this automation quickly leads to large amounts of items being stored away in containers such as &6Chests&r."
		""
		"As you keep adding more Chests to store everything, things can easily become messy and hard to manage. Finding specific items starts taking longer, and moving items around becomes tedious."
		""
		"Fortunately, Create offers tools that help you organize your items much more efficiently. In this chapter, you will learn how to use them to build a proper storage system."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Let’s start by moving all your items into an &6Item Vault&r. Item Vaults work similarly to &6Barrels&r, but they can be expanded to increase their total storage capacity."
		""
		"Unlike most storage containers, Item Vaults do not allow you to manually take items out. You can still insert items manually using an &6Item Hatch&r, but extracting items requires another method."
		""
		"One simple option is to place an &6Andesite Funnel&r on the Item Vault with a &6Depot&r underneath it. This works, but you cannot choose which item is extracted, and items are only extracted one at a time."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/vault.png width:200 height:175 align:center}"
	]
	quest.0BC9416C2B7C8D5E.quest_subtitle: "Storing Large Amounts of Items"
	quest.0BC9416C2B7C8D5E.title: "Item Vaults"
	quest.0FCE59079C96C2DA.quest_subtitle: "Summoning a Destructive Force"
	quest.0FCE59079C96C2DA.title: "The Wither"
	quest.0FD72E185770D0D9.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mechanical Arm&r can transfer up to a full stack of items at once between different selected locations."
		""
		"It can take items from or deposit items into various blocks within a 5-block radius of where it is placed. The order in which it visits its targets depends on its configured behavior and the order in which the blocks were selected during placement."
		""
		"One useful application of the Mechanical Arm is automatically supplying fuel to &6Blaze Burners&r, keeping them running without manual input."
	]
	quest.0FD72E185770D0D9.quest_subtitle: "Moving Items with Precision"
	quest.0FD72E185770D0D9.title: "The Mechanical Arm"
	quest.111712D85DA82D96.quest_subtitle: "Mastering Fluids and Flow"
	quest.111712D85DA82D96.title: "Completing the Copper Age"
	quest.11F9B295CF26283D.quest_desc: [
		"At some point in your Survival world, you will run into the problem of not having enough food. So it’s time to set up a sustainable way to produce it. What if Create could automate that for you?"
		""
		"When attached to a moving &6Contraption&r, &6Mechanical Harvesters&r automatically harvest fully grown crops as they pass over them. Any harvested items are stored directly in containers attached to the Contraption. "
		""
		"For many crops, Mechanical Harvesters can also replant them automatically, making them ideal for sustainable farms."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"A &6Gantry Carriage&r moves back and forth along &6Gantry Shafts&r, depending on the direction and speed of the &6Rotational Force&r it receives."
		""
		"By building a Contraption on top of the Gantry Carriage and attaching Mechanical Harvesters to it, you can create a machine that moves across your crop farm and harvests crops automatically."
		""
		"Take a look at the final pages for images showing an example of this setup."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Redstone Contacts&r emit a Redstone signal when two of them face each other, even if one is part of a moving &6Contraption&r."
		""
		"Now imagine combining this with a &6Gearshift&r. When the Gantry Carriage reaches the end of its path, its Redstone Contact can align with a stationary one and emit a signal. This signal can power a Gearshift, causing the Gantry Carriage to reverse direction and travel back the way it came."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The only drawback is that it can be a hassle to route a Redstone signal directly to the Gearshift. This is where &6Redstone Links&r come in. They allow you to transmit Redstone signals wirelessly within a range of 256 blocks."
		""
		"Right-click a Redstone Link with a &6Wrench&r to switch between transmitting and receiving mode, which determines whether it sends a signal or listens for one. You can also assign each Redstone Link a &6Frequency&r. A transmitting Redstone Link will only communicate with receiving ones that are set to the same Frequency."
		""
		"Combine this with a &6Powered Toggle Latch&r to remotely switch the Gearshift between its powered and unpowered states."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"One last problem remains: how do you automatically get items out of the Contraption? This is where the &6Portable Storage Interfaces&r come in. They allow items to be transferred between a moving Contraption and a stationary storage system without deactivating the &6Movement Anchor&r and disassembling the Contraption."
		""
		"Keep in mind that Portable Storage Interfaces only provide the connection. They do not move items on their own. You will still need a way to transfer items in and out, such as with &6Chutes&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/cropfarm3.png width:200 height:150 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/cropfarm2.png width:200 height:150 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/cropfarm1.png width:200 height:150 align:center}"
	]
	quest.11F9B295CF26283D.quest_subtitle: "Automated Farming with Moving Machines"
	quest.11F9B295CF26283D.title: "Mechanical Harvesters"
	quest.1451D41EF37C713D.quest_desc: [
		"&6/sethome&r saves your current location as your \"home\". You can return to this location from anywhere by typing &6/home&r. To delete your home, use &6/delhome&r."
		""
		"&6/back&r teleports you to your previous location. &6/spawn&r teleports you to the world spawn. Use &6/rtp&r to teleport to a random location in the world."
		""
		"Use &6/warp&r to teleport to a fixed location from a predefined list. Note that only admins can manage warps."
		""
		"Use &6/tpa [playername]&r to request teleporting to another player, or &6/tpahere [playername]&r to request that they teleport to you. These requests can be accepted or denied by the other player."
	]
	quest.1451D41EF37C713D.quest_subtitle: "Basic Teleportation Commands"
	quest.1451D41EF37C713D.title: "FTB Essentials"
	quest.155799872A0BC865.quest_desc: [
		"Imagine you have just finished an intensive mining session and collected a large amount of &6Raw Ores&r that need to be smelted. Processing them one by one in a Furnace can take a long time and quickly becomes tedious."
		""
		"This is where the &6Encased Fan&r comes in. On its own, it creates an airflow that can push or pull entities, depending on the direction in which it rotates. However, it can also be used for &6Bulk Item Processing&r, one of the core methods of automation in Create."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"If you place water, lava, or fire in front of the &6Encased Fan&r, the airflow passing through it will take on its properties. This \"modified\" airflow can then be used to process items that pass through it."
		""
		"Note that the airflow can pass through non-solid blocks such as iron bars and fences. The block placed in front of the Encased Fan determines which type of Bulk Processing is applied."
		""
		"Many items can be processed in multiple ways using Bulk Item Processing. Hover over the Encased Fan and press &6U&r to view all available recipes in &6JEI&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To smelt your Raw Ores, place an Encased Fan facing lava and let it blow air through it toward a &6Depot&r. Then place your Raw Ores on the Depot, and they will be processed automatically after a short time. This method, known as &6Bulk Blasting&r, makes smelting Raw Ores much faster."
		""
		"Take a look at the next page for an example of this setup."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/bulk_smelting.png width:200 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.155799872A0BC865.quest_subtitle: "Bulk Item Processing"
	quest.155799872A0BC865.title: "The Encased Fan"
	quest.169059DFCB8C9A9F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Ancient Tomes&r are used to increase an enchantment’s level by one. What makes them special is that they allow enchantments to go one level above their normal maximum level. Ancient Tomes are rarely found in dungeons and Stronghold libraries."
		""
		"To use one, apply the Ancient Tome to the item using an &6Anvil&r. The item must already have the enchantment at its maximum level for it to become &6Overleveled&r."
		""
		"Fun fact: A Netherite Pickaxe with &6Efficiency VI&r and &6Haste II&r can instantly mine Deepslate."
	]
	quest.169059DFCB8C9A9F.quest_subtitle: "Overleveling Your Enchantments"
	quest.169059DFCB8C9A9F.title: "Ancient Tomes"
	quest.18E18AB83350A90B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pneumatic Tubes&r can transport up to a full stack of items at a time. Their flexible design lets you route them freely through your builds, bending and curving around obstacles."
		""
		"To place a Pneumatic Tube, begin by placing its first end. Then place the second end at the desired destination. Both ends must be placed without switching to another item, as doing so will cancel the connection."
		""
		"Make sure both ends face the correct direction, since Pneumatic Tubes cannot be rotated after placement."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Once both ends have been placed, a line with a single &6Node&r will appear, previewing the path the Pneumatic Tube will follow."
		""
		"By looking at the Node and holding right-click, you can drag it to adjust the path. You can also add additional Nodes, giving the Pneumatic Tube more points at which it can bend or curve."
		""
		"When the line turns green, the path is valid. Press &6Enter&r to confirm the placement."
	]
	quest.18E18AB83350A90B.quest_subtitle: "Transporting Items Through Tubes"
	quest.18E18AB83350A90B.title: "Pneumatic Tubes"
	quest.1B0C39CF4FE359F7.quest_desc: [
		"As you generate &6Rotational Force&r, you will need a way to relay it to where it is needed. As mentioned before, Rotational Force is transferred through physical components. One of the simplest ways to do this is with &6Shafts&r, which relay Rotational Force in a straight line."
		""
		"&6Cogwheels&r and &6Large Cogwheels&r can relay Rotational Force in several different ways, depending on how you arrange them."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The simplest method is called &6adjacent interlocking&r, where two standard Cogwheels are placed directly next to each other."
		""
		"You can also create &6perpendicular interlocking&r by connecting two Large Cogwheels at a 90-degree angle, allowing Rotational Force to be relayed around a corner."
		""
		"Finally, there is &6diagonal interlocking&r, where a Large Cogwheel connects diagonally to a standard Cogwheel. This setup changes the &6Rotational Speed&r: the Large Cogwheel rotates at half the speed relative to the standard Cogwheel"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Encased Chain Drives&r offer another way to relay &6Rotational Force&r."
		""
		"Although they may look similar, Encased Chain Drives have an important advantage over standard &6Cogwheels&r. Each pair of interlocking Cogwheels reverses the direction of rotation, while connected Encased Chain Drives preserve the same rotation direction and speed throughout the chain."
		""
		"The &6Encased Chain Cogwheel&r works like a regular Encased Chain Drive, but also allows direct connection to a Cogwheel or Large Cogwheel."
	]
	quest.1B0C39CF4FE359F7.quest_subtitle: "Simple Ways to Relay Rotational Force"
	quest.1B0C39CF4FE359F7.title: "Cogwheels and Shafts"
	quest.1B4AA2DDEFB4535F.quest_desc: [
		"Whenever you die, a &6Gravestone&r will appear at your death location, containing all your items. Break the Gravestone to retrieve them."
		""
		"When you die, you will receive an &6Obituary&r. This small pamphlet contains information about your death, so keep it with you until you have recovered your items from the Gravestone."
		""
		"You can use the &6/back&r command to return to the location where you died."
	]
	quest.1B4AA2DDEFB4535F.quest_subtitle: "Keeping Your Items Safe After Death"
	quest.1B4AA2DDEFB4535F.title: "The Gravestone"
	quest.1BF390EB035A71D2.quest_desc: [
		"If you don't want to rely on water to generate Rotational Force, you can build a &6Windmill&r using a &6Windmill Bearing&r."
		""
		"Windmills are scalable, meaning you can increase their &6Stress Capacity&r by making them larger. For every eight sail-type blocks added, the Windmill’s output increases by 512 SU and 1 RPM. You can scale a Windmill up to a maximum of 128 sail-type blocks, producing 8192 SU at 16 RPM."
		""
		"Take a look at the next page to see an example of a simple Windmill build."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/windmill.png width:200 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.1BF390EB035A71D2.quest_subtitle: "Generating Power from Wind"
	quest.1BF390EB035A71D2.title: "The Windmill Bearing"
	quest.1D5CCFFFE798541C.quest_subtitle: "Reliable Protection"
	quest.1D5CCFFFE798541C.title: "Iron Armor"
	quest.203F0A91958D3197.quest_desc: [
		"Ever wanted to open your own shop? &6Table Cloths&r make that possible by letting you sell items to other players."
		""
		"Start by setting up a separate &6Logistics Network&r, like the one from the previous quest, to serve as the shop’s inventory. Make sure to lock the &6Stock Keeper&r so other players cannot access its interface and place their own Orders. A locked Stock Keeper can still accept &6Shopping Lists&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Right-click the &6Stock Keeper&r with a Table Cloth to configure it. In this interface, select which items you want to sell and in what quantities, just like when placing an Order. Then click \"Configure\" to confirm. From now on, this Stock Keeper will serve as your &6Shop Keeper&r."
		""
		"Place the configured Table Cloth on a block. The items you chose to sell will be displayed on top of it. Place an item in the empty price slot to choose what players must pay, then hold right-click to adjust the required quantity."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Other players can now interact with the &6Table Cloth&r using an empty hand to create a &6Shopping List&r. This list records which items they want to buy, their quantities, and the total price. "
		""
		"Players can interact with multiple Table Cloths to add items to the same Shopping List, allowing them to purchase everything at once. "
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Once the &6Shopping List&r is ready, the player gives it to the &6Shop Keeper&r. If they can afford the purchase, the Shop Keeper will take the payment and request the purchased items from the Logistics Network. The items will then be packed into a &6Package&r and sent to the pick-up point."
		""
		"You can retrieve the collected payment by interacting with the &6Stock Ticker&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/shop.png width:200 height:150 align:center}"
	]
	quest.203F0A91958D3197.quest_subtitle: "Selling Items with a Shop Keeper"
	quest.203F0A91958D3197.title: "Table Cloths"
	quest.20FF9B6B6F79313D.quest_subtitle: "Mastering Trains and Tracks"
	quest.20FF9B6B6F79313D.title: "Completing the Locomotive Age"
	quest.23072DEC2ABE00F3.quest_subtitle: "Mining in the Deepslate Depths"
	quest.23072DEC2ABE00F3.title: "Cobbled Deepslate"
	quest.24C81D3968448D98.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Gearshift&r reverses the direction of rotation when powered with Redstone."
		""
		"The &6Clutch&r stops relaying Rotational Force when powered with Redstone, acting like a togglable clutch."
		""
		"Both components also come in &6Inverted&r versions, which are activated by default unless they are powered with Redstone."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &6Adjustable Chain Gearshift&r lets you change &6Rotational Speed&r in a way similar to diagonal interlocking between a Large Cogwheel and a standard Cogwheel. It only works when placed as part of an &6Encased Chain Drive&r line, and its effect depends on whether it is directly connected to the Kinetic Source."
		""
		"To craft an Adjustable Chain Gearshift, you will need &6Polished Rose Quartz&r. Hold &6Sand Paper&r in one hand and &6Rose Quartz&r in the other, then hold right-click to polish it."
	]
	quest.24C81D3968448D98.quest_subtitle: "Controlling Rotational Force"
	quest.24C81D3968448D98.title: "The Clutch and the Gearshift"
	quest.261CE9B059156DF7.quest_desc: [
		"Let’s move on to the &6Locomotive Age&r, one of the most exciting ages of Create! This age introduces &6Train Casings&r, which are used to build &6Train Contraptions&r. Over time, these let you design an entire railway network, making it much easier to transport players, items, and fluids across long distances."
		""
		"To begin, place some &6Train Tracks&r. Trains can only travel along these Tracks. Train Tracks can even pass through a &6Nether Portal&r, making it possible for trains to travel between dimensions."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Next, place a &6Train Station&r beside a straight section of Train Track. Train Stations act as fixed stopping points within your railway network and are also used to assemble or disassemble trains."
		""
		"Open the Train Station’s interface and select \"Create New Train\". Then place a &6Train Casing&r on the highlighted section of Train Track. It will automatically turn into a &6Train Bogey&r, which forms the base of a carriage."
		""
		"Before placing a Train Casing, hold it and press &6Left Alt&r to open a menu. This lets you choose between different Bogey designs, which mainly change the train’s appearance."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To make the train longer, add more Bogeys. Each carriage can use either one or two Bogeys, while multiple separate carriages can be connected to form a longer train. If two bogeys should belong to the same carriage, glue them together so they assemble as one unit."
		""
		"Just like other &6Contraptions&r in Create, you can design trains however you want, as long as all required components are included."
		""
		"Every train must have at least one set of forward-facing &6Train Controls&r. Place a &6Seat&r directly behind the Train Controls. This makes manual driving easier and provides a place for a Conductor when the train is automated, which will be explained in the next quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Once you are happy with the design, return to the Train Station’s interface and select \"Assemble Train\". If you later want to change the design, bring the train back to a Train Station and select \"Disassemble Train\" to turn it back into individual blocks."
		""
		"After assembling the train, sit in the Seat and right-click the Train Controls to begin driving. Use &6W&r to accelerate, &6S&r to brake or reverse, and hold &6Space&r when approaching a Station to stop there. When the Tracks split, hold &6A&r or &6D&r to choose which path the train will take."
		""
		"Trains can travel at up to 28 blocks per second. If you attach a storage container holding fuel, such as coal in &6Chests&r or lava in &6Fuel Tanks&r, the train becomes \"powered\" and its maximum speed increases to 40 blocks per second."
	]
	quest.261CE9B059156DF7.quest_subtitle: "Build and Drive Your First Train"
	quest.261CE9B059156DF7.title: "The Train Station and Train Tracks"
	quest.2622FDB116FA61DB.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to &6Everyone Creates&r!"
		""
		"This &6Create&r-focused modpack is designed so everyone can play Create together, whether you are completely new to Create or already an experienced engineer."
		""
		"If you are new, the &6Quest Book&r will guide you step by step through Create’s core mechanics, starting with the basics and gradually expanding from there."
		""
		"If you are already familiar with Create, you can mostly ignore the Quest Book and simply enjoy the modpack on its own."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Create&r is a tech mod focused on mechanical engineering, aesthetic automation, and creativity."
		""
		"Rather than relying only on &6Redstone&r, Create gives you a new set of tools that let you automate your world in a more interactive and visually engaging way."
		""
		"With Create, you build the machines yourself, from simple contraptions to sprawling factories. Dig massive tunnels using automated drills, harvest crops with self-running farms, and even build full-sized trains that travel across your world."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"So basically, Create is all about exploring what you can build and how far you can push your own imagination. Don’t worry if things don’t work perfectly the first time. Create is built around experimentation, and many solutions can work in different ways."
		""
		"Above this quest, you will notice &6Create’s Logo&r. Clicking it will open a YouTube link to the mod’s official trailer, titled \"&6This is Create&r\". It shows what Create is capable of, and what it truly means to explore and push your own imagination."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Progression in this modpack is divided into different &6Ages&r of Create. Each Age has its own chapter in the Quest Book. All chapters can be found in the menu on the far-left side of the &6Quest Window&r."
		""
		"Quests themselves share a similar structure. The &6Tasks&r show what is needed to complete the quest, and the &6Rewards&r show what you can claim after completing it."
		""
		"Not all chapters and quests may be available right away. Some are locked behind a &6Dependency&r, meaning a previous quest must be completed before the next one unlocks. Keep this in mind when navigating the different chapters."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"One of Create’s most helpful features is the &6Ponder&r system. Most Create items can be pondered by hovering over the item in your inventory (or in JEI) and holding &6W&r."
		""
		"Pondering an item opens an in-game visual guide that shows how the component works and how it can be used. These step-by-step visuals are a great way to understand how each part fits into the bigger picture, especially if you are encountering it for the first time."
		""
		"Make regular use of Ponder while progressing through the quests. The quests are written to complement the Ponder guides, not to replace them."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Without further ado, let’s begin your mechanical engineering adventure!"
		""
		"As a reward for this introduction, you can claim the &6Engineer’s Goggles&r. Their full functionality will be explained later, but for now, equipping them marks your first step into the world of Create engineering."
		""
		"You can equip the Engineer’s Goggles in the &6Curios Inventory&r, opened with the &6Curios&r button next to your helmet slot."
		""
		"Note: Completing this quest unlocks the &6Andesite Age&r chapter, which can be found under the &6Time to Create&r chapter group."
	]
	quest.2622FDB116FA61DB.quest_subtitle: "Let's Get Started"
	quest.2622FDB116FA61DB.title: "Everyone Creates"
	quest.26DD20BAA27FA67E.quest_desc: [
		"Instead of chopping down a tree by breaking its logs one by one, you can fell the entire tree by repeatedly breaking the bottom-most log. "
		""
		"The tree will only break after a certain number of &6chops&r, depending on its size. Bigger trees require more total chops, but fewer chops per block."
		""
		"Hold &6Shift&r when breaking a log block to break it normally."
	]
	quest.26DD20BAA27FA67E.quest_subtitle: "Chopping Down Whole Trees"
	quest.26DD20BAA27FA67E.title: "HT's TreeChop"
	quest.293D7E117E609B43.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Extendo Grip&r increases your reach distance, letting you interact with and place blocks from farther away."
		""
		"Equip it in your &6Off-Hand&r while holding the item you want to use in your &6Main-Hand&r."
		""
		"The Extendo Grip normally loses durability with each use. You can prevent this by supplying it with &6Pressurized Air&r from a &6Backtank&r. The Extendo Grip will consume Pressurized Air instead of durability."
	]
	quest.293D7E117E609B43.quest_subtitle: "Extending Your Reach"
	quest.293D7E117E609B43.title: "The Extendo Grip"
	quest.2A107984DE0F52AC.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Backpack&r gives you extra inventory space and can be equipped with several functionality &6Upgrades&r."
		""
		"Equip the Backpack through the &6Curios Inventory&r. Once equipped, press &6B&r to open it at any time."
		""
		"Backpacks come in multiple &6Tiers&r, ranging from Leather to Netherite. Upgrading your Backpack increases its storage capacity."
	]
	quest.2A107984DE0F52AC.quest_subtitle: "Portable Storage"
	quest.2A107984DE0F52AC.title: "Sophisticated Backpack"
	quest.2D340F2E9BC715F4.quest_desc: [
		"With the Mechanical Press, you can now press &6Copper&r into &6Copper Sheets&r, allowing you to progress into the next age of Create: the &6Copper Age&r."
		""
		"The Copper Age introduces a new set of tools mainly used for working with fluids, making fluid handling much more practical."
		""
		"&6Copper Casings&r form the base of many of Create’s fluid-related mechanical components. They are crafted in the same way as Andesite Casings: right-click a &6Stripped Log&r while holding a &6Copper Ingot&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Now imagine you have a large lake of water that you need to empty quickly. The &6Hose Pulley&r helps you fill or drain large bodies of fluid, such as lakes or even lava pools."
		""
		"To move fluids from one location to another, you can use &6Fluid Pipes&r. Fluid Pipes do not move fluids on their own; a &6Mechanical Pump&r is required to create a flow through them."
		""
		"If a body of fluid contains at least &610,000&r source blocks, the Hose Pulley treats it as a bottomless source. This means that you can draw from it endlessly without draining the source itself. "
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Lastly, you will need a way to store large amounts of fluid. This is where &6Fluid Tanks&r come in. They can connect to Fluid Pipes from any side. "
		""
		"Depending on the direction of the flow, the pipes can either insert fluid into or extract fluid from Fluid Tanks."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Note that you cannot interact manually with the fluids inside a Fluid Tank. "
		""
		"To empty a fluid-containing item, such as a Water Bucket, use an &6Item Drain&r. "
		""
		"To fill a compatible item, such as a Glass Bottle, with fluid from the Fluid Tank, use a &6Spout&r. "
		""
		"Both components must be connected to the Fluid Tank through Fluid Pipes, with a Mechanical Pump directing the flow where needed."
	]
	quest.2D340F2E9BC715F4.quest_subtitle: "Storing and Moving Fluids"
	quest.2D340F2E9BC715F4.title: "Fluid Tanks"
	quest.2FA5714EA4642C21.quest_desc: [
		"Wish you had Creative flight in Survival? The &6Jetpack&r might be the solution; it lets you fly using &6Pressurized Air&r."
		""
		"Equip the Jetpack in your chest slot. Press &6G&r to activate or deactivate it, and press &6H&r to toggle &6Hover Mode&r."
		""
		"Hover Mode maintains your altitude without letting you fall. This is especially useful while building, but it consumes Pressurized Air more quickly."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"When sprint-swimming underwater, the Jetpack boosts your swimming speed. Hover Mode also prevents you from slowly sinking."
		""
		"If you have an &6Elytra&r equipped in your back slot, the Jetpack can provide a continuous firework-like boost while you hold &6Space&r."
		""
		"Just like a &6Copper Backtank&r, the Jetpack can also supply tools with &6Pressurized Air&r when they require it."
	]
	quest.2FA5714EA4642C21.quest_subtitle: "Flying Using Pressurized Air"
	quest.2FA5714EA4642C21.title: "The Jetpack"
	quest.30183ED60C62985C.quest_subtitle: "Mining Through the Stone Layer"
	quest.30183ED60C62985C.title: "Cobblestone"
	quest.30FBD7C96ECE7A2E.quest_subtitle: "Eternal Void"
	quest.30FBD7C96ECE7A2E.title: "The End"
	quest.311AD64349AB8211.quest_desc: [
		"Remember the automatic crop farm from the &6Andesite Age&r? Imagine you want to keep track of how much &6Wheat&r is currently stored after being harvested. You could check the storage manually, but that quickly becomes impractical. Instead, you can let a &6Smart Observer&r monitor it for you."
		""
		"When placed against a storage container, a Smart Observer reads what is stored inside that container. You can choose whether it counts everything in the container or only a specific item."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To make this information visible, you can use a &6Display Link&r. A Display Link reads information from a &6Display Source&r, such as a Smart Observer, and sends it to a &6Display Target&r, such as a &6Display Board&r."
		""
		"Besides the Smart Observer, many other blocks can act as Display Sources. For example, placing a Display Link on an &6Andesite Tunnel&r or &6Brass Tunnel&r allows it to measure how many items pass through it per second, minute, or hour. This can be used to track the production rate of your farm."
		""
		"You can also display information from components such as a &6Speedometer&r or &6Stressometer&r."
	]
	quest.311AD64349AB8211.quest_subtitle: "Making Production Visible"
	quest.311AD64349AB8211.title: "The Smart Observer"
	quest.3187CE56D441FA5A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Copycat Blocks&r can take on the appearance and properties of other blocks while keeping their own shape and size. They are crafted from &6Zinc Ingots&r using a &6Stonecutter&r."
		""
		"To change the appearance of a Copycat Block, right-click it with the block you want it to copy. Right-click it again with the same block to cycle through different texture orientations."
		""
		"Some Copycat Blocks are &6stackable&r. Right-clicking a placed Copycat Block with another of the same type will enlarge it. Hold &6Shift&r while hovering over a Copycat Block in your inventory to see whether it can be stacked."
	]
	quest.3187CE56D441FA5A.quest_subtitle: "Decorative Blocks With Custom Shapes"
	quest.3187CE56D441FA5A.title: "Copycat Blocks"
	quest.3213E97150D54E52.quest_desc: [
		"&6Farmer’s Delight&r gently expands on farming and cooking in Minecraft by adding new crops and simple, immersive ways to prepare food."
		""
		"The &6Cooking Pot&r is the main workstation of Farmer’s Delight. When placed above a heat source, such as a &6Stove&r, it allows you to combine ingredients into cooked meals. These meals often restore a large amount of hunger, and sometimes give the &6Nourishment&r or &6Comfort&r effect."
		""
		"&6Knives&r are used to cut and prepare ingredients. Place an ingredient on a &6Cutting Board&r, then right-click it with a Knife to process it."
	]
	quest.3213E97150D54E52.quest_subtitle: "Expanding on Farming and Cooking"
	quest.3213E97150D54E52.title: "Farmer's Delight"
	quest.344010DF14146C14.quest_desc: [
		"You have probably already noticed the &6Minimap&r, but did you know there is also a &6World Map&r? You can open it by pressing &6M&r."
		""
		"Just like with the Minimap, you can press &6-&r to zoom out and &6+&r to zoom in while viewing the World Map."
		""
		"Right-click anywhere on the World Map to open a menu with several options, including the option to create a &6Waypoint&r. You can manage your waypoints in the &6Waypoint Screen&r, which you can open by pressing &6J&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"In the World Map, you can also claim nearby &6Chunks&r. Claimed chunks are protected, preventing other players from placing, breaking, or interacting with blocks within them."
		""
		"To claim a chunk, simply right-click it and press &6Claim Selected&r. You can also select multiple chunks to claim them all at once. Unclaiming works the same way: select your claimed chunks, right-click, and press &6Unclaim Selected&r."
		""
		"You can also use the command &6/openpac-claims claim&r to claim the chunk you are standing in, and &6/openpac-claims unclaim&r to unclaim the chunk you are standing in."
	]
	quest.344010DF14146C14.quest_subtitle: "Navigating the World and Protecting Your Land"
	quest.344010DF14146C14.title: "Xaero's Minimap and World Map"
	quest.3483E53665BBBD3A.quest_desc: ["The &6Trading Post&r lets you trade with all &6Villagers&r within a 24-block horizontal and 16-block vertical range through its interface."]
	quest.3483E53665BBBD3A.quest_subtitle: "Villages Unlike Any Other"
	quest.3483E53665BBBD3A.title: "Integrated Villages"
	quest.35251A8E8E94D28A.quest_desc: [
		"Let’s explore two ways to generate &6Rotational Force&r that are \"self-sustaining\", so you don’t have to stand there cranking them forever."
		""
		"&6Water Wheels&r generate Rotational Force when water flows across them. They are one of the earliest and most reliable &6Kinetic Sources&r you can build."
		""
		"The &6Large Water Wheel&r provides twice the &6Stress Capacity&r of the standard version, but spins at only half the speed."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"When multiple &6Kinetic Sources&r are connected to the same network, their &6Stress Capacities&r combine. At the same time, the highest &6Rotational Speed&r among them sets the speed for the entire network."
		""
		"For example, placing Large Water Wheels in series with a standard Water Wheel gives you the higher Stress Capacity of the Large Water Wheels while benefiting from the higher speed of the standard Water Wheel."
		""
		"Take a look at the next page to see an example of a simple Water Wheel setup."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/waterwheels.png width:200 height:150 align:center}"
	]
	quest.35251A8E8E94D28A.quest_subtitle: "Generating Power with Flowing Water"
	quest.35251A8E8E94D28A.title: "Water Wheels"
	quest.35D2672B95A9255F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Hydraulic Transmission&r can relay &6Rotational Force&r between two connected ends. Its flexible design makes it easy to route Rotational Force through your builds, letting the tube bend and curve as needed."
		""
		"However, this convenience comes at a cost. Hydraulic Transmissions are expensive to craft, making them better suited for specific setups rather than everyday use."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To place a Hydraulic Transmission, begin by placing its first end. Then place the second end at the desired destination. Both ends must be placed without switching to another item, as doing so will cancel the connection."
		""
		"Make sure both ends face the correct direction, since Hydraulic Transmissions cannot be rotated after placement."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Once both ends are placed, a line with a single &6Node&r will appear, previewing the path the Hydraulic Transmission will take."
		""
		"By looking at the Node and holding right-click, you can drag it to adjust the path. You can also add additional Nodes, giving the Hydraulic Transmission more points at which it can bend or curve."
		""
		"When the line turns green, the path is valid. Press &6Enter&r to confirm the placement."
	]
	quest.35D2672B95A9255F.quest_subtitle: "An Easy but Expensive Way to Relay Rotational Force"
	quest.35D2672B95A9255F.title: "The Hydraulic Transmission"
	quest.392C8B7EE404388B.quest_subtitle: "Entering the Mother’s Lair"
	quest.392C8B7EE404388B.title: "The Ender Dragon"
	quest.393C171C4D31B1D1.quest_desc: [
		"So &6Train Contraptions&r are already powerful when it comes to transportation. They can move items, fluids, and players across long distances with ease."
		""
		"Besides being useful, trains also look impressive, which is part of what makes the &6Locomotive Age&r so exciting."
		""
		"In the previous quest, you learned how to build and drive a Train Contraption. Now let’s make trains even more useful by automating them."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"A mob &6Seated&r directly behind the &6Train Controls&r, or a &6Blaze Burner&r placed directly behind the Train Controls, can drive the train for you. To do this, they need a &6Train Schedule&r, which assigns them as a &6Train Driver&r."
		""
		"To set up a Train Schedule, right-click it while holding it in your main hand to open its menu. Here, you can add actions such as \"Travel to Station\"."
		""
		"Create a sequence of actions, then right-click the seated mob or Blaze Burner to give the Train Driver the completed Train Schedule. It will then follow the Schedule automatically."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"As mentioned before, &6Train Contraptions&r can also transport items and fluids across long distances. This works in the same way as with other Contraptions: use &6Portable Storage Interfaces&r for items and &6Portable Fluid Interfaces&r for fluids."
		""
		"Keep in mind that these Interfaces only create the connection between the train and the stationary cargo system. You will still need components such as Funnels, Chutes, Fluid Pipes, or Mechanical Pumps to move the items or fluids."
		""
		"A scheduled train can stop at a station while cargo is loaded or unloaded, and &6Schedule Conditions&r can determine when it departs. For example, you can make a train wait until its cargo has been unloaded or until a set amount of time has passed."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Automating multiple trains on the same railway network can cause problems when they share the same &6Train Tracks&r. Without proper control, trains may collide."
		""
		"To prevent this, you will need to use &6Train Signals&r. Train Tracks between two Train Signals form a segment, which becomes occupied when a train enters it. Automated trains will wait before entering an occupied segment, preventing multiple trains from using the same section at once."
		""
		"&6Semaphores&r can be placed on top of Train Signals to visually indicate whether a section is currently occupied."
	]
	quest.393C171C4D31B1D1.quest_subtitle: "From Manual Control to Automation"
	quest.393C171C4D31B1D1.title: "The Train Schedule"
	quest.394F617CA2364356.quest_desc: [
		"Let’s dive deeper into automation and take it a step further with Automated &6Shaped Crafting&r."
		""
		"Using a &6Mechanical Mixer&r and &6Basin&r, you can already automate Shapeless recipes. When combined with a &6Mechanical Press&r, the Basin can also perform Compacting recipes."
		""
		"However, some recipes require items to be arranged in a specific pattern, also known as Shaped Crafting. These recipes need a different approach to automation, which is where &6Mechanical Crafters&r come in."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Mechanical Crafters&r are not only useful for automating Shaped Crafting, but can also form crafting grids larger than the standard 3×3 grid of a regular &6Crafting Table&r."
		""
		"Some advanced recipes, such as the one for &6Crushing Wheels&r, require this kind of large-scale crafting."
	]
	quest.394F617CA2364356.quest_subtitle: "Automating Shaped Crafting Recipes"
	quest.394F617CA2364356.title: "Mechanical Crafters"
	quest.3B177511E540C6A4.quest_desc: [
		"You have probably used &6Pistons&r before, maybe even to build a piston door. However, vanilla Pistons have clear limitations. This is where the &6Mechanical Piston&r becomes useful."
		""
		"Unlike vanilla Pistons, Mechanical Pistons can extend much farther using &6Piston Extension Poles&r. With &6Super Glue&r, they can also push or pull entire structures as moving Contraptions."
		""
		"The direction in which a Mechanical Piston moves depends on the direction of the applied &6Rotational Force&r. To reverse its movement, you can use a &6Gearshift&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The only drawback is that it can be a hassle to route a Redstone signal directly to the Gearshift. This is where &6Redstone Links&r come in. They allow you to transmit Redstone signals wirelessly within a range of 256 blocks."
		""
		"Right-click a Redstone Link with a &6Wrench&r to switch between transmitting and receiving mode, which determines whether it sends a signal or listens for one. You can also assign each Redstone Link a &6Frequency&r. A transmitting Redstone Link will only communicate with receiving ones that are set to the same Frequency."
		""
		"Combine this with a &6Powered Toggle Latch&r to remotely switch the Gearshift between its powered and unpowered states."
	]
	quest.3B177511E540C6A4.quest_subtitle: "Better than Vanilla Pistons"
	quest.3B177511E540C6A4.title: "The Sticky Mechanical Piston"
	quest.3B3619B23F76C854.quest_desc: [
		"&6Soul Beads&r are dropped by &6Wraiths&r, neutral mobs that spawn in &6Soul Sand Valleys&r."
		""
		"Right-clicking the Soul Bead releases the soul trapped inside, which will fly in the direction of the nearest &6Nether Fortress&r."
	]
	quest.3B3619B23F76C854.quest_subtitle: "Fiery Depths"
	quest.3B3619B23F76C854.title: "The Nether"
	quest.3B660147BC248FAC.quest_subtitle: "Mastering Storage and Logistics"
	quest.3B660147BC248FAC.title: "Completing Post Production"
	quest.3B91008EEB4422D2.quest_desc: [
		"After a big mining trip, it is time to smelt your &6Raw Ores&r into usable &6Ingots&r. We are not going to cover Bulk Blasting again. Instead, let’s look at a more efficient way to process Raw Ores while also increasing their yield."
		""
		"A pair of &6Crushing Wheels&r can crush Raw Ores into &6Crushed Ores&r, giving each Raw Ore a 10% chance to produce an additional Crushed Ore. Make sure both Crushing Wheels rotate toward each other for them to work properly."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Crushed Ores can then be processed using &6Bulk Washing&r, producing the corresponding Nuggets along with a high chance of additional byproducts. These Nuggets can be compacted into Ingots by placing them in a &6Basin&r beneath a &6Mechanical Press&r."
		""
		"Since this process can produce several different outputs, you will need a way to sort them. &6Brass Funnels&r and &6Brass Tunnels&r include filter slots, giving you precise control over which items can pass through them. You can filter for a specific item or use an &6Item Filter&r or &6Attribute Filter&r."
		""
		"Note: Completing this quest unlocks the &6Locomotive Age&r chapter."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/ore4.png width:200 height:175 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/ore1.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/ore2.png width:200 height:150 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/ore3.png width:200 height:175 align:center}"
	]
	quest.3B91008EEB4422D2.quest_subtitle: "Improving Ore Processing"
	quest.3B91008EEB4422D2.title: "Crushing Wheels"
	quest.3C94E955C0650F25.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you have mastered the basics, it is time to enter the &6Brass Age&r. Components made from Brass are \"smarter\" than their Andesite counterparts, giving you more control over your machines and making more complex forms of automation possible."
		""
		"Brass is created by combining &6Copper&r and &6Zinc&r in a &6Mechanical Mixer&r. This recipe requires the &6Basin&r to be heated using a &6Blaze Burner&r."
		""
		"Obtain a Blaze Burner by right-clicking a Blaze with an &6Empty Blaze Burner&r to capture it. This means you will need to travel to the &6Nether&r before you can progress into the Brass Age."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Brass is also used to craft &6Brass Casings&r, which form the base of many advanced mechanical components. "
		""
		"Just like Andesite and Copper Casings, they are made by right-clicking a &6Stripped Log&r while holding a Brass Ingot."
	]
	quest.3C94E955C0650F25.quest_subtitle: "Producing Brass in a Heated Basin"
	quest.3C94E955C0650F25.title: "The Blaze Burner"
	quest.3DC5F03A080D4A6A.quest_desc: [
		"As your Survival world grows, there comes a point where you constantly need wood. Chopping trees by hand quickly becomes repetitive, so why not automate the process?"
		""
		"&6Mechanical Saws&r have two main functions. They can automate Stonecutting and Sawmill recipes, and they can also cut down entire trees."
		""
		"Back in the &6Andesite Age&r, you could already build an automatic tree farm, but you still had to replant &6Saplings&r by hand. This is where &6Deployers&r become useful."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Start with the foundation of your tree farm. A &6Mechanical Bearing&r rotates an attached structure when supplied with Rotational Force. By combining it with &6Mechanical Saws&r and &6Deployers&r, you can build a circular tree farm."
		""
		"When Deployers are part of a &6Contraption&r, they can use items stored in attached containers. Set the Deployer’s filter to &6Saplings&r so it replants them as the Contraption moves around the farm."
		""
		"The Mechanical Saws will cut down fully grown trees, while the harvested items are collected in containers attached to the Contraption."
		""
		"Take a look at the images on the next pages for an example build."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/tree1.png width:200 height:200 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/tree2.png width:200 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.3DC5F03A080D4A6A.quest_subtitle: "Building an Automatic Tree Farm"
	quest.3DC5F03A080D4A6A.title: "Mechanical Saws"
	quest.3F9D6E645D62DFCF.quest_desc: [
		"As you progress, you will often end up with large amounts of the same items, whether from farming, mining, or exploration. Processing these items by hand can quickly become slow and repetitive."
		""
		"&6Contraptions&r are only one part of what Create can do. You can also automate crafting steps, build processing systems, and combine them into complete production lines. "
		""
		"In this quest, you will learn how to turn a steady input of &6Wheat&r into &6Bread&r automatically, from start to finish."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Let’s begin with &6Andesite Funnels&r. These can insert items into or extract items from a container, such as a &6Chest&r."
		""
		"A &6Mechanical Belt&r works like a conveyor belt, moving items between containers, machines, or other belts. When combined with Andesite Funnels, items can automatically be taken from or placed into a container."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"In this example, the Wheat is collected by a farming Contraption and transferred through a Portable Storage Interface."
		""
		"The &6Portable Storage Interface&r allows items to be transferred between a moving Contraption and a stationary storage system. Use an Andesite Funnel and a Mechanical Belt to move the Wheat from the Portable Storage Interface into a storage container."
		""
		"Next, transport the Wheat along another Mechanical Belt into a &6Millstone&r. The Millstone grinds simple items into their processed forms, such as turning Cobblestone into Gravel or &6Wheat&r into &6Wheat Flour&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Remember &6Bulk Item Processing&r using an &6Encased Fan&r and a &6Depot&r? Items can also be processed while travelling along a Mechanical Belt. "
		""
		"Position Encased Fans so their modified airflow passes across the Mechanical Belt. First, use water to turn Wheat Flour into Dough through &6Bulk Washing&r. Then use fire to bake the Dough into Bread through &6Bulk Smoking&r."
		""
		"Take a look at the following pages for an example of this production line."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/bread1.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/bread15.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/bread2.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/bread3.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
	]
	quest.3F9D6E645D62DFCF.quest_subtitle: "From Farm to Factory"
	quest.3F9D6E645D62DFCF.title: "Mechanical Belts"
	quest.446A069EE0DED5E9.quest_subtitle: "Magical Imbuement of Your Equipment"
	quest.446A069EE0DED5E9.title: "The Enchanting Table"
	quest.484FAE518B86BE2E.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you know the basics of Create’s power system, it’s time to actually generate &6Rotational Force&r. The simplest way to do this early on is with a &6Hand Crank&r. It is easy to use, but inefficient and only provides a small amount of &6Stress Capacity&r."
		""
		"To craft a Hand Crank, you will need &6Andesite Alloy&r, one of the most important early-game materials in Create."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Andesite Alloy is also used to craft &6Andesite Casings&r, which are required for almost every basic mechanical component."
		""
		"To make an Andesite Casing, right-click a &6Stripped Log&r while holding Andesite Alloy to turn it into an Andesite Casing."
	]
	quest.484FAE518B86BE2E.quest_subtitle: "Create’s Most Important Resource"
	quest.484FAE518B86BE2E.title: "Andesite Alloy"
	quest.48F2E8E7EFE90D99.quest_desc: [
		"Setting up &6Bulk Item Processing&r can sometimes be a hassle, especially with flowing lava or when dealing with non-solid blocks. So let’s try it again with the &6Fan Catalyst&r, which makes setting up Bulk Item Processing a lot easier."
		""
		"Place the &6Empty Fan Catalyst&r in front of an Encased Fan, then right-click it with Lava, Water, Netherrack, or Soul Sand to give it the processing properties you need."
	]
	quest.48F2E8E7EFE90D99.quest_subtitle: "Simplifying Bulk Item Processing"
	quest.48F2E8E7EFE90D99.title: "Fan Catalysts"
	quest.4912C85A00C9461E.quest_desc: [
		"One useful feature of &6Fluid Tanks&r is that they can be attached to moving Contraptions. &6Portable Fluid Interfaces&r allow fluids to be transferred into or out of these tanks without disassembling the Contraption."
		""
		"When a Portable Fluid Interface on a moving Contraption connects with a stationary one, the Contraption can temporarily exchange fluids with external Fluid Tanks. Keep in mind that Portable Fluid Interfaces only create the connection. They do not move fluids on their own. You will still need a &6Mechanical Pump&r to move fluid through the &6Fluid Pipes&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There is one important limitation. When multiple Fluid Tanks are attached to a Contraption, the &6Portable Fluid Interface&r treats them as a single combined tank. This means that if the Contraption contains multiple types of fluid, regular Fluid Pipes cannot choose which specific fluid to extract."
		""
		"This is where the &6Smart Fluid Pipe&r comes in. It lets you set a filter that determines which type of fluid can flow through the pipe, making it possible to separate different fluids."
	]
	quest.4912C85A00C9461E.quest_subtitle: "Handling Fluids on Contraptions"
	quest.4912C85A00C9461E.title: "Portable Fluid Interface"
	quest.4C02726BF1C7DD53.quest_subtitle: "Mastering the Basics"
	quest.4C02726BF1C7DD53.title: "Completing the Andesite Age"
	quest.4CAEA2E62B1C78A5.quest_desc: [
		"Sometimes you may want a faster way to travel between different parts of your base or between nearby buildings. This is where &6Hypertubes&r come in: enclosed tubes that let you travel at great speed."
		""
		"The &6Hypertube Entrance Block&r acts as both an entry and exit point. From there, &6Hypertube Blocks&r extend the tube in any direction. This flexible building system lets you shape Hypertubes into straight lines, curves, or loops, making them as long or as short as needed."
		""
		"The &6Hypertube Accelerator Block&r changes the speed at which you travel through a Hypertube, letting you speed up or slow down along the route."
	]
	quest.4CAEA2E62B1C78A5.quest_subtitle: "Traveling at High Speed Through Tubes"
	quest.4CAEA2E62B1C78A5.title: "Hypertubes"
	quest.50308A86F77915C4.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Tool Belt&r lets you quickly switch between tools. Hold &6R&r to open its menu, then click an empty slot to store the tool from your main hand."
		""
		"Retrieve a stored tool in the same way by clicking a filled slot. If you are already holding a tool, it will automatically swap with the one in the Tool Belt."
		""
		"&6Belt Pouches&r are used to increase how many tools the Tool Belt can hold. Apply them using an Anvil."
	]
	quest.50308A86F77915C4.quest_subtitle: "Easy Acces to Tools"
	quest.5060E93702AC81ED.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mechanical Mixer&r is another way to process items in Create. It is mainly used to produce &6Brass&r, but can also automate Shapeless Crafting and Brewing. Place it above a &6Basin&r and make sure it is supplied with enough &6Rotational Speed&r to operate."
		""
		"One useful early-game recipe is producing &6Andesite Alloy&r with the Mechanical Mixer. Combining one Iron or Zinc Nugget with one Andesite produces one Andesite Alloy."
		""
		"Note: Completing this quest unlocks the &6Brass Age&r chapter."
	]
	quest.5060E93702AC81ED.quest_subtitle: "The Next Step in Item Processing"
	quest.5060E93702AC81ED.title: "The Mechanical Mixer"
	quest.50E0097656349F7F.quest_desc: [
		"Let’s say you’ve built a complete railway network and want a clear way to display information about it. Regular &6Display Boards&r can show basic information, but they are limited when it comes to detailed railway information."
		""
		"This is where &6Advanced Display Boards&r come in. They are designed specifically for trains and stations."
		""
		"Advanced Display Boards can show detailed information about departing trains, such as their platform, line, and possible delays. They can also be placed directly on trains to show information such as the next stop or final destination."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"After placing an &6Advanced Display Board&r, right-click it with a &6Wrench&r to open the Advanced Display Settings. Here, you can choose which type of information the board should display."
		""
		"Multiple Advanced Display Boards can be connected to form a larger display, as long as they are all configured to use the same display type."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"When an Advanced Display Board is part of a &6Train Contraption&r and configured with the correct display type, it will automatically show information about the train’s route. After assembling the train or changing its Schedule, it may take one complete &6Train Schedule&r cycle before the displayed information updates correctly."
		""
		"To use an Advanced Display Board at a station, connect it to the &6Train Station&r using a &6Display Link&r. When configuring the Display Link, select \"Advanced Displays\" as its target."
	]
	quest.50E0097656349F7F.quest_subtitle: "Visualizing Your Train Network"
	quest.50E0097656349F7F.title: "Advanced Display Boards"
	quest.528145CA7FAD6E2D.quest_subtitle: "Power Drawn from the Nether Star"
	quest.528145CA7FAD6E2D.title: "The Beacon"
	quest.53A001A49A115E65.quest_desc: [
		"The longer you play in Survival, the more &6Experience&r you gain. In vanilla Minecraft, there is no practical way to store your Experience, which means that when you die, you lose almost all of it."
		""
		"Luckily, &6Create: Enchantment Industry&r adds new tools and methods for handling Experience and Enchantments within Create, including a way to safely store your Experience."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &6Experience Lantern&r absorbs Experience either from a nearby player or from &6Experience Orbs&r within its range. It converts this Experience into &6Liquid Experience&r, which can be stored and transported like any other fluid. "
		""
		"The Experience Lantern also works on moving Contraptions. Any collected Experience will be stored in attached &6Fluid Tanks&r."
		""
		"Alternatively, you can store and retrieve Experience manually using the &6Experience Hatch&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Items enchanted with &6Mending&r can also be repaired automatically. Supply a &6Spout&r with &6Liquid Experience&r and let it pour onto a damaged item with Mending placed underneath."
		""
		"The Spout will pour only the amount of Liquid Experience needed to repair the item."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &6Mechanical Grindstone&r functions as an automated Grindstone. It can convert &6Nuggets of Experience&r and &6Blocks of Experience&r back into Liquid Experience. It can also extract Enchantments from items and convert them into Liquid Experience."
		""
		"Fun fact: Mobs killed using a &6Deployer&r or &6Crushing Wheels&r will drop Nuggets of Experience."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To convert Liquid Experience back into &6Experience&r, pump it out of a Fluid Tank into open air using a &6Mechanical Pump&r. The Liquid Experience will turn back into &6Experience Orbs&r that you can collect."
		""
		"In this setup, the &6Fluid Valve&r is a useful control tool. It lets you open or close the flow through Fluid Pipes and can be operated using a &6Copper Valve Handle&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Liquid Experience can do more than just store Experience. By using a &6Printer&r, you can copy &6Enchanted Books&r and even &6Ancient Tomes&r."
		""
		"To do this, insert the Enchanted Book into the Printer, supply it with &6Liquid Experience&r, and place a regular book underneath. The Printer will then create a copy of the Enchanted Book."
		""
		"The Printer can also copy written books. For this, you will need &6Ink&r instead of Liquid Experience."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/experience.png width:175 height:200 align:center}"
	]
	quest.53A001A49A115E65.quest_subtitle: "Turning Experience into a Fluid"
	quest.53A001A49A115E65.title: "The Experience Lantern"
	quest.54C1DF75FA76352D.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Deployer&r is one of the highlights of the &6Brass Age&r, opening up a wide range of new automation possibilities."
		""
		"The Deployer can simulate a player’s left-click and right-click actions. It can place blocks, use items on blocks, interact with components, and even attack entities. Many tasks that would normally require manual interaction can therefore be automated."
		""
		"Deployers also work while attached to moving &6Contraptions&r, making them especially useful for automated building machines, farms, and other dynamic automation setups."
	]
	quest.54C1DF75FA76352D.quest_subtitle: "Mimicking Player Actions"
	quest.54C1DF75FA76352D.title: "The Deployer"
	quest.5618ECDE2EE2B9F5.quest_desc: [
		"In the previous quests, you learned the basics of Create’s resources and mechanics. Now it is time to take the next step by introducing &6Contraptions&r."
		""
		"Contraptions are custom-built structures that can move as a single unit. Once assembled, the entire build behaves like one moving object that can travel, rotate, and perform actions such as mining, building, farming, or transporting items."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"A Contraption is assembled by a mechanical component that acts as its &6Movement Anchor&r. When activated, the Movement Anchor gathers the blocks attached to it and assembles them into one moving unit."
		""
		"Common examples of Movement Anchors include the Rope Pulley, the Gantry Carriage, and even the Windmill Bearing. Each one moves a Contraption in a different way, but they all follow the same basic principle: the Movement Anchor assembles the attached structure and determines how it moves."
		""
		"When the Movement Anchor stops or is deactivated, the Contraption can disassemble back into individual blocks."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"For blocks to move together as part of a Contraption, they must be properly attached to the Movement Anchor. This is where &6Super Glue&r comes in."
		""
		"Super Glue binds the touching faces of blocks together, causing them to be treated as one connected structure when the Contraption is assembled."
		""
		"Some blocks, such as &6Linear Chassis&r, can automatically attach to nearby blocks. Others, such as Chests or decorative blocks, may need to be manually glued so they move along with the rest of the Contraption."
	]
	quest.5618ECDE2EE2B9F5.quest_subtitle: "Bringing Your Builds to Life"
	quest.5618ECDE2EE2B9F5.title: "Super Glue"
	quest.5663BD2A3C3D48AE.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Rotation Speed Controller&r lets you precisely adjust the speed of &6Rotational Force&r."
		""
		"To use it, place a &6Large Cogwheel&r on top of the Controller. Depending on how it is connected to the rest of the network, the Cogwheel acts as either the input or the output."
	]
	quest.5663BD2A3C3D48AE.quest_subtitle: "Precisely Adjusting Rotational Speed"
	quest.5663BD2A3C3D48AE.title: "The Rotation Speed Controller"
	quest.5679B457E656C53F.quest_desc: [
		"Let’s say you’ve built something in a Creative world and want to recreate it in Survival. Instead of rebuilding it by hand, let the &6Schematicannon&r do the work."
		""
		"The Schematicannon can automatically rebuild structures that have been saved as &6Schematics&r."
		""
		"To begin, craft a &6Schematic and Quill&r. This tool lets you save a structure by selecting two opposite corners, marking out a 3D area. Once the area is selected, give the schematic a name and save it for later use."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Next, place a &6Schematic Table&r and open its interface. Insert an &6Empty Schematic&r into the left slot, then browse through your saved structures."
		""
		"Choose the structure you want and confirm your selection. This writes the saved structure onto the Empty Schematic, turning it into a usable &6Schematic&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"With your prepared Schematic in hand, right-click in the world to preview its placement. You can move and rotate the preview until it lines up exactly where you want the structure to be built."
		""
		"Once everything looks right, place the &6Schematicannon&r nearby. Insert the Schematic into its input slot and add &6Gunpowder&r to the fuel slot. Each piece of Gunpowder allows the cannon to place roughly 400 blocks."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Next, place containers such as Chests next to the Schematicannon and fill them with the materials required for the build."
		""
		"If you are unsure which materials are needed, insert a &6Clipboard&r into the cannon’s Checklist Printer slot. This will print a &6Material Checklist&r that you can use as a reference."
		""
		"When everything is stocked and ready, press the start button in the cannon’s interface. The Schematicannon will begin rebuilding the structure automatically, layer by layer, launching blocks into place until the build is complete."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Also, check out &6CreateMod.com&r, the \"Create Schematics Repository\". There, you can download Schematics made by other players or upload and share your own."
	]
	quest.5679B457E656C53F.quest_subtitle: "Building from Blueprints"
	quest.5679B457E656C53F.title: "The Schematicannon"
	quest.5722227ADE87F88A.quest_desc: [
		"Imagine you are storing all the Cobblestone you collect inside &6Item Vaults&r. Over time, you keep storing more and more, perhaps even expanding the storage with additional Item Vaults. Eventually, you reach a point where you realize you have enough."
		""
		"The question then becomes: how do you stop storing more than you actually need, while still keeping a certain amount available? This is where the &6Threshold Switch&r comes in."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &6Threshold Switch&r monitors how many items are stored inside a storage container and converts that information into a &6Redstone&r signal."
		""
		"In its interface, you can set two values: an upper threshold and a lower threshold. When the number of items reaches the upper threshold, the Threshold Switch turns its Redstone signal on. That signal remains active until the item count drops below the lower threshold, at which point it turns off again."
		""
		"The Threshold Switch can also be configured to count only a specific item, instead of everything stored inside the container."
	]
	quest.5722227ADE87F88A.quest_subtitle: "Preventing Storage Overflow"
	quest.5722227ADE87F88A.title: "The Threshold Switch"
	quest.5A3A341F529D5DB9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Large Cogwheels&r are not the only way to change the axis along which Rotational Force is relayed."
		""
		"A standard &6Gearbox&r relays Rotational Force in all four horizontal directions. If you need to relay it vertically, right-click the Gearbox with a &6Wrench&r to turn it into a &6Vertical Gearbox&r."
		""
		"Regular Gearboxes reverse the direction of rotation when relaying it around a corner. &6Parallel Gearboxes&r, however, preserve the same direction of rotation across all corner connections."
	]
	quest.5A3A341F529D5DB9.quest_subtitle: "Relaying Rotational Force in All Directions"
	quest.5A3A341F529D5DB9.title: "Gearboxes"
	quest.5B3ACE9C9E4AF5D6.quest_desc: [
		"In the previous quest, you were introduced to &6Package Frogports&r and the &6Chain Conveyor&r, which allow you to easily transport &6Packages&r. This method is very convenient over short distances, but becomes less practical as the distance increases."
		""
		"That is where the &6Postbox&r comes in. Postboxes use &6Train Contraptions&r to transport Packages, making them much more practical over long distances and even between dimensions."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Before placing a Postbox, right-click a &6Train Station&r while holding it in your main hand to link the Postbox to that Train Station. Place it within four blocks of the linked Train Station, then give it a unique name that serves as its &6Address&r."
		""
		"When a &6Train Contraption&r with an attached inventory stops at the linked Train Station, the Postbox can transfer Packages to and from the train. Packages whose address does not match the Postbox can be loaded onto the train, while Packages with a matching address are unloaded into the Postbox."
		""
		"By adding specific instructions to a &6Train Schedule&r, trains can automatically collect Packages and deliver them to Postboxes linked to other Train Stations."
	]
	quest.5B3ACE9C9E4AF5D6.quest_subtitle: "Delivering Packages by Train"
	quest.5B3ACE9C9E4AF5D6.title: "The Postbox"
	quest.5B529559F80AFED0.quest_desc: [
		"Water Wheels and Windmills work well for smaller builds, but eventually you will need a much higher &6Stress Capacity&r. Building more and more of them quickly becomes impractical, so let’s take a look at the &6Steam Engine&r instead."
		""
		"When properly built and maintained, a Steam Engine can generate a large amount of &6Rotational Force&r using heat and water."
		""
		"Attaching a Steam Engine to a Fluid Tank turns the tank into a &6Boiler&r. When heat is applied from below and enough water is supplied through Fluid Pipes, the Steam Engine activates and begins generating Rotational Force."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"While wearing the &6Engineer’s Goggles&r, you can view detailed information about the Boiler’s status. One important value is the &6Boiler Level&r, which can reach a maximum of 18. The Boiler Level determines how many Steam Engines the Boiler can support at full efficiency."
		""
		"The Boiler Level depends on three factors: the amount of heat applied, the amount of water supplied, and the size of the Boiler. The weakest of these three factors limits the Boiler’s current level."
		""
		"As the Boiler Level increases, it can support more Steam Engines and provide a greater amount of &6Stress Capacity&r, making Steam Engines a powerful and scalable Kinetic Source."
	]
	quest.5B529559F80AFED0.quest_subtitle: "Generating Power with Steam"
	quest.5B529559F80AFED0.title: "The Steam Engine"
	quest.5E3B89D9CF1E4F8C.quest_desc: [
		"Experience is usually used to enchant items with an &6Enchanting Table&r. But what if you could use &6Liquid Experience&r instead?"
		""
		"The &6Blaze Enchanter&r works similarly to an Enchanting Table. Supply it with Liquid Experience from below, then insert an enchantable item to enchant it."
		""
		"On the side of the Blaze Enchanter, you can set the &6Enchantment Level&r. This determines how strong and rare the applied enchantments will be. In vanilla Minecraft, the maximum Enchantment Level is 30."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Placing an enchantable item into the slot on the side of the Blaze Enchanter activates &6Template Enchanting Mode&r. The item acts as a reference, meaning the Blaze Enchanter will only apply enchantments that are valid for that type of item."
		""
		"To enchant items using Template Enchanting Mode, you will need an &6Enchanting Template&r. Once enchanted, an Enchanting Template can be used in an Anvil to apply its enchantments to a desired item. Doing so consumes the Enchanting Template."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &6Blaze Forger&r works similarly to an Anvil. Supply it with &6Liquid Experience&r from below to activate it."
		""
		"The Blaze Forger can merge enchantments from two matching items, just like an Anvil, but without increasing their Repair Cost. It can also merge &6Enchanting Templates&r."
		""
		"One particularly useful feature of the Blaze Forger is its ability to extract enchantments from an item and transfer them onto a blank Enchanting Template."
	]
	quest.5E3B89D9CF1E4F8C.quest_subtitle: "Beyond the Enchanting Table"
	quest.5E3B89D9CF1E4F8C.title: "Blaze Enchanter and Blaze Forger"
	quest.5FCF8B2D37D9B26F.quest_desc: [
		"One of the mechanical components crafted using &6Andesite Casings&r is the &6Mechanical Press&r. It is one of Create’s basic processing machines."
		""
		"The Mechanical Press is mainly used to press ingots into &6Sheets&r and create &6Cardboard&r. When placed above a &6Basin&r, it can also be used for Compacting and Packing. Be sure to check &6JEI&r to see all available recipes."
		""
		"Note: Completing this quest unlocks the &6Copper Age&r and &6Post Production&r chapters."
	]
	quest.5FCF8B2D37D9B26F.quest_subtitle: "The First Step in Item Processing"
	quest.5FCF8B2D37D9B26F.title: "The Mechanical Press"
	quest.6184FB979CADB8CF.quest_desc: [
		"You've probably noticed the scrollable list of items on the right side of your inventory, with a search bar at the bottom. This is &6Just Enough Items&r (&6JEI&r), a tool that lets you look up items and view their recipes."
		""
		"Hover over an item and press &6R&r to view its recipe, or press &6U&r to see how it is used in other recipes."
		""
		"The search bar is mainly used to look up items, but you can also filter the list using specific prefixes. For example, type \"&6@[modname]&r\" to show only items from a specific mod."
	]
	quest.6184FB979CADB8CF.quest_subtitle: "Your Reference for Crafting Recipes"
	quest.6184FB979CADB8CF.title: "Just Enough Items"
	quest.61A1B955037F5781.quest_desc: [
		"So far, the &6Blaze Enchanter&r and &6Blaze Forger&r have provided new ways to automate and manage Enchantments. However, they can go even further by entering &6Super Enchanting Mode&r."
		""
		"The Blaze Enchanter and Blaze Forger both enter Super Enchanting Mode when given a &6Cake o’ Enchanting&r. Be careful when using this mode, as it summons lightning strikes. Place a &6Lightning Rod&r nearby to safely redirect them. "
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"When the &6Blaze Enchanter&r enters Super Enchanting Mode, its maximum &6Enchantment Level&r is doubled. It can also apply treasure enchantments to items."
		""
		"When the &6Blaze Forger&r enters Super Enchanting Mode, it can overlevel enchantments by merging two of the same enchantment. It can also merge conflicting enchantments."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Using Super Enchanting Mode requires a &6Super Enchanting Template&r."
		""
		"To craft one, you will first need a &6Block of Super Experience&r. This is obtained by letting lightning strike a regular &6Block of Experience&r."
	]
	quest.61A1B955037F5781.quest_subtitle: "Super Enchanting"
	quest.61A1B955037F5781.title: "Cake o' Enchanting"
	quest.625D78A142A0565E.quest_desc: [
		"Mining and building underwater can be quite tedious. Luckily, Create offers a few pieces of equipment that'll help you work and explore beneath the surface."
		""
		"Let’s start with the &6Copper Backtank&r. It stores &6Pressurized Air&r that can be used by certain pieces of equipment."
		""
		"Fill the Copper Backtank with Pressurized Air by placing it in the world and supplying &6Rotational Force&r to the Shaft on top. Keep in mind that the Backtank’s supply is limited. Once it runs out, you will need to refill it before your equipment can continue using it."
		""
		"The &6Capacity&r enchantment increases the amount of Pressurized Air the Backtank can store."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &6Copper Diving Helmet&r is one piece of equipment that uses &6Pressurized Air&r from the Copper Backtank. While supplied, it lets you breathe underwater by gradually consuming the Pressurized Air. The Copper Diving Helmet also grants &6Aqua Affinity&r, making it easier to mine blocks underwater."
		""
		"The &6Copper Diving Boots&r make you sink more quickly and prevent you from swimming normally. In return, they let you walk and jump underwater as if you were on land."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The Copper Backtank, Copper Diving Helmet, and Copper Diving Boots can all be upgraded to &6Netherite&r."
		""
		"When worn together with Netherite Leggings, the complete set provides immunity to fire and lava while slowly consuming &6Pressurized Air&r from the Netherite Backtank. The Netherite Diving Helmet also improves your vision while submerged in lava, making it possible to explore deep beneath the lava oceans of the &6Nether&r."
	]
	quest.625D78A142A0565E.quest_subtitle: "Traversing the Underwater World"
	quest.625D78A142A0565E.title: "The Copper Backtank"
	quest.6497509FF4B6DD43.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Engineer’s Goggles&r you’ve obtained are not just for aesthetics. They let you see useful information about Create’s mechanical components, such as the &6Stress Impact&r of a component or the &6Stress Capacity&r of a Kinetic Source."
		""
		"The &6Speedometer&r and &6Stressometer&r are two components that make especially good use of this feature."
	]
	quest.6497509FF4B6DD43.quest_subtitle: "Monitoring Rotational Force"
	quest.6497509FF4B6DD43.title: "Speedometer and Stressometer"
	quest.668D1FDA7123153F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Vein Mining&r enchantment lets you mine an entire vein of ore by breaking a single block."
		""
		"Simply hold &6Shift&r while mining an ore, and your pickaxe will automatically break all adjacent ore blocks in the same vein."
	]
	quest.668D1FDA7123153F.quest_subtitle: "Superior Protection"
	quest.668D1FDA7123153F.title: "Diamond Armor"
	quest.672F221F6F44215C.quest_desc: [
		"Imagine you're away from your base but still want to receive &6Packages&r from a distance. Without being able to interact with the &6Stock Keeper&r back at your base, how do you request items while you're far away? More importantly, how will those Packages even reach you?"
		""
		"This is where the &6Portable Stock Ticker&r and the &6Robo Bee&r come in. Linking a Portable Stock Ticker to a &6Logistics Network&r lets you place &6Orders&r remotely. Instead of travelling along a Chain Conveyor, the resulting Packages can be delivered directly to you by a Robo Bee."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &6Robo Bee Port&r acts as the hub for these deliveries. After placing one, open its interface and insert at least one &6Robo Bee&r into the designated slot. Each Robo Bee can carry only one Package at a time, but a single Robo Bee Port can hold up to a stack of Robo Bees. This allows multiple Packages to be delivered at the same time using multiple Robo Bees."
		""
		"Next, click the \"+\" button and add yourself to the &6Robo Bee Network&r. Only players who add themselves to this list can receive Packages from that Robo Bee Port, preventing players from spam-sending Packages to others."
		""
		"When placing an Order, use your username as the &6Package Address&r so the Robo Bee knows where to deliver the Package."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &6Portable Stock Ticker&r has effectively unlimited range, meaning you can request items from anywhere in the world as long as you remain in the same dimension."
		""
		"Note that the &6Chunks&r containing the storage connected to the Logistics Network must remain loaded for their items to stay accessible. Robo Bees themselves can continue travelling through unloaded Chunks, although long-distance deliveries may still take some time to arrive."
	]
	quest.672F221F6F44215C.quest_subtitle: "Remote Package Delivery"
	quest.672F221F6F44215C.title: "The Robo Bee"
	quest.673809B7FD96C065.quest_desc: [
		"In Create, machines are powered by &6Rotational Force&r. Think of it as the mechanical version of electricity: a spinning \"energy\" that is transferred through physical components like &6Cogwheels&r and &6Shafts&r instead of wires."
		""
		"These physical components let you see the power moving through your builds; if a component is spinning, it is receiving Rotational Force."
		""
		"Multiple machines can share the same Rotational Force. Together, they form what is known as a &6Kinetic Network&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Rotational Force is measured in &6Stress Units&r, usually shortened to &6SU&r."
		""
		"&6Kinetic Sources&r act like the generators of Create’s power system. Each one provides a certain amount of SU, known as its &6Stress Capacity&r."
		""
		"Machines powered by Rotational Force place a load on the network while they run. This load is known as their &6Stress Impact&r and is also measured in SU."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Separate from SU is &6Rotational Speed&r, which determines how quickly the mechanical components in a network spin. It is measured in &6Rotations Per Minute&r, usually shortened to &6RPM&r, and ranges from 0 to 256 RPM. "
		""
		"The higher the speed, the faster your machines will work. However, increasing the speed also increases their Stress Impact. This is because &6Speed and Stress are directly proportional&r. When you increase the speed, you also increase the load those machines place on the network."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Mechanical components do not consume &6Stress Units&r over time like fuel. Instead, they place a constant load (their &6Stress Impact&r) on the network while they run, meaning they require a fixed amount of SU to operate at a certain speed."
		""
		"To keep everything running, the combined Stress Impact of all connected components must stay within the total &6Stress Capacity&r of your &6Kinetic Sources&r. If the total Stress Impact exceeds that capacity, the network becomes &6Overstressed&r, causing all connected components to stop until the imbalance is fixed."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Let’s sum this up with an example. If a Kinetic Source provides 48 SU of Stress Capacity, and two mechanical components each have a Stress Impact of 16 SU, they place a combined load of 32 SU on the network. This leaves 16 SU of Stress Capacity available, so the network can keep running."
		""
		"Now let’s say you double the speed of both components. Their Stress Impact also doubles from 16 SU to 32 SU each, giving them a combined Stress Impact of 64 SU. Because the total Stress Impact now exceeds the available Stress Capacity of 48 SU, the network becomes Overstressed."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"This may feel like a lot of information to take in at once. You do not need to understand everything perfectly right now, but having a general idea of how Create’s power system works will help as you start building and experimenting. The more you work with it, the more familiar it will become!"
	]
	quest.673809B7FD96C065.quest_subtitle: "Understanding Create’s Power System"
	quest.673809B7FD96C065.title: "Rotational Force"
	quest.6D9D61D6BC3E7EED.quest_desc: [
		"Using &6Mechanical Belts&r to transport &6Packages&r can eventually become quite a hassle. Luckily, Packages can also be transported using the &6Chain Conveyor&r. "
		""
		"Place two Chain Conveyors within 32 blocks of each other, then connect them using &6Chains&r. Chain Conveyors can also be used to relay Rotational Force."
		""
		"You can travel along the Chains by right-clicking them with a &6Wrench&r. You will start hanging and be carried along. Sneak to dismount."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Packages can also travel along the Chains, but they need a way to be put onto the Chains in the first place. This is where the &6Package Frogport&r comes in."
		""
		"Before placing the Package Frogport, select a point on the Chains while holding it in your main hand, then place it on a &6Packager&r. In its interface, give the Package Frogport a unique name, which serves as its &6Address&r."
		""
		"Addresses can be applied to &6Packages&r when they are made by the Packager. The name given to the Package Frogport tells it which Packages it should retrieve from the Chains, since it will only retrieve Packages whose address matches its name."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Let’s place another &6Order&r using this setup. First, build a pick-up point using another Package Frogport and a &6Depot&r. Before sending an order, manually enter the Package’s address in the &6Stock Keeper&r interface. If everything is set up correctly, the Package will be sent to the Package Frogport at the pick-up point."
		""
		"Packages whose address does not match the name of any Package Frogport in the network will endlessly circle on a Chain Conveyor, indicating that they do not have a valid destination."
		""
		"Take a look at the next pages for example images of this setup."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/network1.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/network2.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Transporting Packages this way works much like sending parcels through a postal service, where each parcel ends up at the address written on it. Thinking of it this way makes it clear that the system has many more uses than what has been shown so far. Let’s look at one practical way you can integrate it."
		""
		"Remember the &6Bulk Blasting&r setup from the &6Andesite Age&r? Instead of walking over to it, manually inserting the items, waiting for them to finish, and then retrieving the processed items, you can now let the &6Logistics Network&r handle everything automatically."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Another way to apply an address to a Package is by placing a &6Sign&r against the &6Packager&r with the address written on it. Any Packages created by that Packager will automatically be given that address."
		""
		"Set up a Packager with another &6Package Frogport&r at the Bulk Blasting setup. Packages can be sent directly to it through the &6Stock Keeper&r by entering the name of that Package Frogport as the Package’s address. Once processed, the items can be packed into a Package again and sent back to the Logistics Network."
		""
		"Take a look at the next pages for example images of this setup."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/bulkblasting1.png width:200 height:120 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/bulkblasting2.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
	]
	quest.6D9D61D6BC3E7EED.quest_subtitle: "Routing Packages Through the Network"
	quest.6D9D61D6BC3E7EED.title: "The Package Frogport"
	quest.6E50C83E8B19AD04.quest_desc: [
		"Some items in Create require &6Sequenced Assembly&r to craft. Think of it as a small factory line designed to perform several processing steps in a specific order."
		""
		"One important example is the &6Precision Mechanism&r, which requires its own Sequenced Assembly line."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Sequenced Assembly&r begins with a base item, such as a &6Golden Sheet&r when crafting a Precision Mechanism."
		""
		"The item is placed on a &6Depot&r or moved along a &6Mechanical Belt&r, where it passes through machines such as &6Deployers&r or &6Mechanical Saws&r in the required order. When the base item begins Sequenced Assembly, it turns into an incomplete item."
		""
		"The incomplete item must continue through the remaining stages and may need to repeat the entire sequence several times. With each completed step, it gradually progresses toward the final product."
		""
		"Some Sequenced Assembly recipes also have a chance to fail, producing a different item instead of the intended result."
	]
	quest.6E50C83E8B19AD04.quest_subtitle: "Crafting the Precision Mechanism"
	quest.6E50C83E8B19AD04.title: "Sequenced Assembly"
	quest.713498ADA422C485.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Slicer&r is a machine similar to the Mechanical Mixer and Mechanical Press. It automatically recognizes all cutting recipes from &6Farmer’s Delight&r, acting as an automatic &6Cutting Board&r."
		""
		"To use it, insert the correct tool by right-clicking the Slicer with an applicable item, such as a &6Knife&r. Then place the Slicer above a &6Mechanical Belt&r or a &6Depot&r, and let it process any valid ingredients that pass underneath."
		""
		"Note that any tool used by the Slicer will lose durability over time, so you will eventually need to replace it for the Slicer to keep working."
	]
	quest.713498ADA422C485.quest_subtitle: "Automating Farmer’s Delight"
	quest.713498ADA422C485.title: "The Slicer"
	quest.745FA24E6CEEF194.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Drills&r can break blocks directly in front of them when powered by Rotational Force."
		""
		"What makes them especially useful is that they also function while attached to a moving &6Contraption&r. This allows you to build automated mining machines that move and dig on their own."
		""
		"One simple example is a vertical quarry built using a &6Rope Pulley&r. The Rope Pulley can raise or lower an attached structure. When combined with Mechanical Drills, it can dig straight down, layer by layer, while you sit back and watch."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The direction and speed of the applied Rotational Force determine whether the Rope Pulley raises or lowers the Contraption and how quickly it moves. You can use a &6Clutch&r and &6Gearshift&r to control this."
		""
		"When the &6Pulley Magnet&r makes contact with a properly connected structure, the Rope Pulley assembles it into a Contraption."
		""
		"Take a look at the next page to see an example of this build."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/drill.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
	]
	quest.745FA24E6CEEF194.quest_subtitle: "Letting Machines Do the Digging"
	quest.745FA24E6CEEF194.title: "Mechanical Drills"
	quest.75C77D6F71F9D139.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mechanical Rollers&r are useful tools for terraforming terrain. They can pave paths, flatten terrain, break blocks, or fill empty spaces as a moving &6Contraption&r travels forward."
		""
		"While the Contraption is disassembled, right-click the top of a Mechanical Roller to select its mode. Each mode determines how it interacts with the terrain, such as \"Clear Blocks and Pave\" or \"Straight Fill Below\"."
		""
		"If you choose a mode that places blocks, right-click the top of the Mechanical Roller with the block you want it to use. Make sure the Contraption includes one or more storage containers filled with enough of that material."
	]
	quest.75C77D6F71F9D139.quest_subtitle: "Automated Terrain Shaping"
	quest.75C77D6F71F9D139.title: "Mechanical Rollers"
	quest.77E2BD70D3702127.quest_desc: [
		"While exploring, you will come across these distinctive &6Loot Containers&r."
		""
		"Each one gives every player their own loot when opened, meaning a Loot Container that was already opened by someone else will still contain \"fresh\" loot just for you!"
		""
		"Thanks to &6Lootr&r, there is no longer a race to be the first to explore structures."
	]
	quest.77E2BD70D3702127.quest_subtitle: "Exploring Without Competing for Loot"
	quest.77E2BD70D3702127.title: "Lootr"
	quest.7931D7344546F666.quest_desc: [
		"Chests come in different &6Tiers&r, ranging from Copper to Diamond, each providing increased storage capacity. "
		""
		"You can use &6Chest Upgrades&r on a placed chest to upgrade it without breaking it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Carry On&r allows you to pick up and carry &6Block Entities&r, such as chests, furnaces, and even &6Spawners&r, as well as small &6Mobs&r. "
		""
		"Simply &6Shift + Right-Click&r with empty hands to pick up a Block Entity or Mob. Right-click again to place it down."
		""
		"Keep in mind that you can only carry one Block Entity or Mob at a time, and your movement speed will be reduced depending on the inventory size or the Mob’s size."
	]
	quest.7931D7344546F666.quest_subtitle: "Larger Storage Containers"
	quest.7931D7344546F666.title: "Iron Chests"
	quest.7A26A3EC74C1F56D.quest_desc: ["Note: The Elytra can be equipped in the back slot of the &6Curios Inventory&r, allowing you to wear an Elytra and a Chestplate at the same time."]
	quest.7A26A3EC74C1F56D.quest_subtitle: "Taking to the Skies"
	quest.7A26A3EC74C1F56D.title: "The Elytra"
	quest.7CB4CA747C2363C6.quest_subtitle: "Ultimate Protection"
	quest.7CB4CA747C2363C6.title: "Netherite Armor"
	quest.7DC977C3170D8A0F.quest_desc: [
		"Have you tried building an elevator Contraption using a &6Rope Pulley&r? If so, you probably noticed its main limitation: it moves continuously, making it difficult to stop at specific floors."
		""
		"Let’s try the &6Elevator Pulley&r instead. It is designed to move a structure between fixed stopping points, making it ideal for building elevators that travel between multiple floors."
		""
		"When building an elevator cabin, make sure to include a single horizontal &6Redstone Contact&r. This tells the Elevator Pulley where the cabin is and helps it recognize the stopping points."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Place another &6Redstone Contact&r in front of the cabin’s Contact, facing toward it, to turn it into an &6Elevator Contact&r."
		""
		"Elevator Contacts define the elevator’s \"floors\": the fixed stopping points between which the cabin can travel. Once the first Elevator Contact has been placed, any additional Redstone Contacts placed at the same X and Z coordinates and facing the cabin will automatically become Elevator Contacts as well."
		""
		"Sending a Redstone signal to an Elevator Contact will call the elevator to that floor. Place &6Contraption Controls&r inside the cabin to control the elevator from within."
	]
	quest.7DC977C3170D8A0F.quest_subtitle: "Building a Multi-Floor Elevator"
	quest.7DC977C3170D8A0F.title: "The Elevator Pulley"
	quest.7E6CDD2EFFD406FE.quest_desc: [
		"Tired of strip-mining for Diamonds? Let’s try something different. Instead of digging by hand, you can build a tunnel bore using &6Mechanical Drills&r, which will automatically excavate tunnels as the machine moves forward."
		""
		"Remember how Mechanical Drills break any block in front of them? That same behavior still applies when they are part of a moving &6Contraption&r. This is actually the core idea behind most digging machines, such as the quarry from the Andesite Age."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To give the tunnel bore a more practical way of moving, we will use a &6Cart Assembler&r to assemble it into a Contraption. When you build a structure on top of the Cart Assembler, a Minecart passing through it will \"pick up\" the entire build and turn it into a &6Minecart Contraption&r that can move along &6Rails&r."
		""
		"Minecart Contraptions can be taken into the inventory by right-clicking them with a &6Wrench&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"For the tunnel bore to keep moving, it needs to place &6Rails&r in front of itself and remove them again after passing, so it can continue moving forward without running out of track."
		""
		"Use &6Deployers&r at the front to place Rails ahead of the Contraption. If the tunnel bore crosses gaps, an additional Deployer can place blocks underneath the Rails to support them. Place &6Mechanical Drills&r at the front to break blocks, and a &6Mechanical Plough&r at the back to pick up the Rails after the Minecart has passed."
		""
		"Take a look at the images on the next pages to see an example of a tunnel bore."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/minecart2.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/minecart3.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quests/minecart1.png width:200 height:125 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7E6CDD2EFFD406FE.quest_subtitle: "Mining With a Tunnel Bore"
	quest.7E6CDD2EFFD406FE.title: "Mechanical Drills II"
	quest.7F2A5A2F50AB6BEB.quest_desc: [
		"&6Petrol’s Parts&r introduces several new mechanical components, giving you more ways to relay Rotational Force."
		""
		"Both the &6Coaxial Cogwheel&r and the &6Coaxial Large Cogwheel&r behave like their regular counterparts, but they allow a Shaft to pass through their center while continuing to rotate independently."
		""
		"The &6Corner Shaft&r helps relay Rotational Force around a 90-degree corner."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"When a &6Planetary Gearset&r interlocks with a Large Cogwheel, its outer teeth rotate at the same speed as the Large Cogwheel. However, its central Shaft rotates at twice that speed and in the opposite direction."
		""
		"The &6Differential&r rotates at the average speed when both sides are connected to &6Kinetic Sources&r."
	]
	quest.7F2A5A2F50AB6BEB.quest_subtitle: "More Ways to Relay Rotational Force"
	quest.7F2A5A2F50AB6BEB.title: "Petrol's Parts"
	quest.7FE944B4CE7BB3C7.quest_desc: [
		"Say you want to turn Cobblestone into Stone. With the setup from the previous quest, you could place an Order at the &6Stock Keeper&r and send the Cobblestone to your Bulk Blasting setup. Once it has been processed and returned to the Logistics Network, you could place another Order to retrieve the Stone."
		""
		"That works fine once or twice. However, if you constantly need Stone, placing the same order over and over quickly becomes tedious. So let’s take this setup one step further and use the &6Factory Gauge&r to let the Logistics Network handle it automatically."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &6Factory Gauge&r allows the Logistics Network to monitor the amount of a specific item and automatically take action when that amount drops below a chosen level."
		""
		"The Factory Gauge can be used in two different modes: &6Restocker Mode&r and &6Recipe Mode&r. To begin, right-click the Factory Gauge on the &6Stock Ticker&r to tune it to your Logistics Network."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Restocker Mode&r is used when the &6Factory Gauge&r is placed directly on a &6Packager&r. In this mode, the Factory Gauge monitors the amount of a specific item inside the container connected to that Packager. When the amount falls below the &6Target Amount&r, it requests enough of that item from the Logistics Network to refill the container."
		""
		"The requested items are sent to the &6Target Address&r configured in the Factory Gauge’s interface. This is usually the address of the Package Frogport connected to the same Packager."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Recipe Mode&r is used when the &6Factory Gauge&r is placed anywhere else, such as on a wall for easy overview. In this mode, the Factory Gauge monitors the total amount of a specific item across the entire &6Logistics Network&r."
		""
		"You can imagine that if the monitored item falls below the &6Target Amount&r, there may be nowhere to request more of it from. So instead of simply restocking it, the network needs to produce the item by sending other available items for processing or crafting. This can be done by setting up &6Factory Tasks&r, which tell the Logistics Network which items are required and what item should be produced."
		""
		"This may sound complex at first, so let’s walk through it using the example of turning Cobblestone into Stone."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Start by placing one Factory Gauge and configuring it to monitor &6Stone&r. This will act as the output Gauge. Place a second Factory Gauge nearby and configure it to monitor &6Cobblestone&r. This will act as the input Gauge."
		""
		"You now need to tell the Logistics Network that Stone is produced from Cobblestone. To do this, open the interface of the Factory Gauge monitoring Stone, select \"Add new connection\", then right-click the Factory Gauge monitoring Cobblestone to add it as an input."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"In the interface of the Factory Gauge monitoring Stone, you can now see which item is used as the input and which item is expected as the output. Here, you can also adjust how much Cobblestone is used and how much Stone is expected in return. Make sure the input and output amounts match how your setup processes the items."
		""
		"Next, set the &6Target Address&r where the input items should be sent. In this case, the address should point to the Bulk Blasting setup, where Cobblestone is turned into Stone."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Finally, set a &6Target Amount&r for Stone. As long as the total amount of Stone in the Logistics Network remains at or above this value, the Factory Gauge stays inactive. When the amount falls below the Target Amount, it requests the required Cobblestone and sends it to the Bulk Blasting setup."
		""
		"While the task is running, the Factory Gauge records the expected Stone as a &6Promise&r. This prevents it from repeatedly sending more Cobblestone while the previous batch is still being processed."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The connection between the &6Factory Gauges&r changes color to show its current state."
		""
		"A dark blue connection means the output Gauge is requesting its inputs, while light blue means those inputs have been promised. Green means the &6Target Amount&r has been reached."
		""
		"A gray connection is inactive, while a blinking red connection means that one or more required inputs cannot be found in the Logistics Network."
	]
	quest.7FE944B4CE7BB3C7.quest_subtitle: "Setting Up Factory Tasks"
	quest.7FE944B4CE7BB3C7.title: "Factory Gauges"
